{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And HaShem, He is the one who goes before you, etc.</b> And He did not say 'your Elohim,' in the manner that He said to Israel (Deuteronomy 31:3), because His name, may He be blessed, is not singled out upon the righteous in his own vitality (Tanḥuma Toldot 7), but upon the totality of Israel His name is singled out, as He said (Exodus 20:2): ״אָנֹכִי ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ״." "And His saying <b>He is the one who goes.</b> And it was not sufficient to say 'and HaShem goes before you,' to alert that one should not consider by the capacity found in Israel to destroy, for He is able to overcome all the battles prepared before him, because the matter does not depend on their capacity, but on HaShem alone it depends, and thus He said ״He is the one who goes,״ and not in partnership with another force." "<b>He will be with you.</b> He said ״He״ — to inform that the great degree, which is the totality of the Shekhinah that goes before the camp of Israel, this degree will be with him. And thus He said ״He will be with you״ — meaning, the aspect mentioned immediately above."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {1 "The text reads לִשְׁמֹר in brackets corrected to לִשְׁמֹד ('to destroy'), apparently a scribal variant; rendered according to the corrected reading."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:20:44.857403771Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}